# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your Supabase project's values
# (Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API). Placeholders only: never
# commit real values (.env* is git-ignored; this file is the exception).
#
# VITE_ variables are inlined into the browser bundle, so they may only hold
# values that are safe to publish. The anon / publishable key is public by
# design, but it is NOT access control: Row Level Security is.
# Never put a secret (service_role key, Gemini key, ...) behind a VITE_ name.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Supabase service-role key — SERVER-ONLY. Used by the serverless functions in
# api/ (batches, inventory, ...). It bypasses Row Level Security, so keep it
# out of the browser and out of git: set it in Vercel (Sensitive) or in your
# shell for a local `vercel dev`, never with a VITE_ prefix.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Gemini AI (free tier) — server-only. Get a key at
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey and add it in Vercel → Settings →
# Environment Variables. Do NOT prefix with VITE_: that would ship the key
# to every visitor's browser.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Optional: override the default model (gemini-3.8-flash).
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# Kill switch for stock on log (Phase 8). Unset: POST /api/batches takes a
# Pro user's oil out of stock as it logs the batch. "client": the server
# leaves stock alone and the app deducts the old way (PATCH /api/inventory).
# STOCK_ON_LOG=client

# CORS: the API answers browsers only from the origins listed in
# api/_lib/http.ts (the production aliases). Add a custom domain there.
